Verse 1

[C] He's got the Eye of Fatima on the [Am] wall of his room.
Two [C] bottles of tequila, three [Am] cats and a broom.
He's got an [Bb] 18-year-old angel
and she's [F] all dressed in black.
[A] [Bb] [B] 
He's got [C] 15 bindles of [Bb] cocaine tied up in a [G] sack.
 

Verse 2

[C] And this here's a government experiment
and we're [Am] driving like Hell.
To get some [C] cowboys some acid and to [Am] stay in motels.
We're gonna [Bb] eat up some wide open spaces
Like it was a [F] cruise on the Nile.
[A] [Bb] [B] 
Take the [C] hands off the clock,
we're gonna [Bb] be here a [G] while. 

Verse 3

And [C] I am the Eye of Fatima
on the [Am] wall of the motel room.
And [C] cowboys on acid are like [Am] Egyptian cartoons.
[Bb] And no one ever conquered Wyoming
from the [F] left or from the right.
[A] [Bb] [B] 
But you can [C] stay in motel [Bb] rooms and stay up all [G] night.
